				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/completeindie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5632962); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5632962&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607826039" alt="CompleteIndie" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5632962)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/completeindie" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5632962); return false;" >CompleteIndie</a></span> <span class="odate time_1607826003 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">13 Dec 2020 02:20</span>
																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-50742/per-page-discussions">Per Page Discussions / Per page discussions</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/scp-4857/comments/show">SCP-4857</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843392">
									

<p>I love this. I'm a sucker for the more psychological horrors, like <a href="/scp-3001">SCP-3001</a>, the ones that use emotion to fuck with you. It's amazing, and it's honestly chilling in a nice way.</p>
<p>As a reader, I'd personally want Blue to be right: that the entire anomaly is just an anomalous divider between the groups. But in reality, it's like Model Red, because otherwise&#8230;</p>
<p>But you can't know. No one does. And if Ehwez tries to figure it out, it could spell completely disaster.</p>
<p>The line that best sums this up is this:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>We could be sitting on a landmine, or on a cushion, and either way it would really be a poor idea to get up right now.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>My only complaint is the Model Blue and Model Red coloring in the object class is a bit unfriendly (the rest of the colored text has context). I'd add a small footnote to the Object Class, but that's it.</p>
<p>Good job!</p>

							</div>

								
					
