																	<br/>
						in discussion <a href="/forum/c-88827/foundation-universe">SCP Universe / Foundation Universe</a> &raquo;
						<a href="/forum/t-13894838/i-d-rather-be-part-of-the-serpent-s-hand-than-the-foundation">I&#039;d Rather Be Part of the Serpent&#039;s Hand Than the Foundation&quot;</a>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843388">
									

<p>I've thought about this several times, and I could never be loyal to the SCP Foundation as it stands in-universe. The Foundation commits human rights violations without a second thought at every turn, even when completely unnecessary, and their fundamental approach to the anomalous is flawed. For every -EX, there are a dozen &quot;unexplained&quot; anomalies which are totally understood by the Foundation's understanding of science and could easily be added to current sciences. Memetics, the multiverse, and <a href="/scp-439">SCP-439</a> jump to mind pretty quickly.</p>

							</div>

								
					
