														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843377">
									

<p>I vaguely remember Makuta in the second movie being too campy for me to take seriously. Roodaka scared the living daylights out of me as a kid though, especially in the scene where she's talking to Vakama about how loyal her horde is. She straight-up tells a bunch of visorak to jump off a tower and they immediately do just that and that scarred me a bit as a kid.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>they were all far better than any toy-inspired direct-to-video animated movie has any right to be.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This. They had visorak blink independently and even had a janitor visorak cleaning the floor in the foreground of one of the scenes. It's insane how well-animated the movies are for that time.</p>

