														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4843363">
									

<p>Thank you for reviewing my concept. I was aware that a few SCPs dealt with Christian-like concepts of Hell, though I had not seen SCP-4661 or Arcadia.</p>
<p>My plan was to use a detached, clinical tone in Containment Procedures and Description, and then to use a slightly more narrative, direct style in a string of Exploration Logs, Interviews, and Incident Reports.</p>
<p>The SCP would include descriptions of how MTFs dealt with manifesting demons (I was being facetious with the &quot;badass demon-killing&quot;), as well as researchers' notes on these entities. But the main focus would be on the people exploring &quot;Hell&quot; (the Foundation would refer to it as the Abyss.)</p>
<p>Over several interview logs, the Mediums who access the SCP would try to explain what they see. The Mediums, who are of several faiths: Christian, Jewish, Islamic, Hindu, Buddhist; would experience the Abyss in different ways, since it is a metaphysical reality, and the human mind often needs to visualize and familiarize abstract concepts. What the Mediums see is often dark and traumatic, and repeated visits to the Abyss often eat away at their mental health.</p>
<p>Interviewing researchers do find a common theme among the Mediums' varying accounts: the horror of the Abyss is self-imposed. More than a simple torture chamber, the souls and entities within are locked in personal reveries, tortured by their own insanity, loneliness, and self-hatred as they constantly relive horrific fantasies and tear each other apart.</p>
<p>I agree that disturbing visuals alone can't carry an article. The central horror in this article is conceptual; existential. The visuals serve to fully realize that; to turn the scary idea into a tangible nightmare.</p>
<p>I had intended for the SCP itself: the Portals, Virgil Events, and such, to be rather mysterious. Mediums always experience some kind of Lobby or Antechamber. This room is manned by a figure in a white mask, (dubbed SCP-XXXX-A) who guides the visitor to the soul they ask for, and/or lets them explore Hell, but never explains itself. I would be happy to go more into this part of the SCP if you think that would improve the article.</p>
<p>As for the Chaos Insurgency, I only mention it once. A dead spy who had information the Foundation needed was a good motive for it to start using this SCP. Is there a problem in using the Insurgency?</p>
<p>P.S.: Is MTF Psi-8 &quot;Silencers&quot; the right group for this SCP?</p>

							</div>

								
					
